{
  "_comment": "QM-0011 cross-family resolver conformance corpus. One table asserting that every architecture plugin resolves what it claims and returns `unknown` for everything else (NSIR-001, NSIR-006, NSIR-008, MVP-08). Exercised by crates/q-nsir/tests/resolver_conformance.rs. This file is NOT a plugin manifest: Registry::load_dir looks for `<dir>/plugin.toml` under each subdirectory, so a plain file here is skipped, which `loading_from_the_repo_directory_matches_the_builtins` still proves.",

  "_schema": "Top-level keys are plugin ids, except keys beginning with `_`, which are metadata and are never treated as a family. A family maps to an array of rows. A POSITIVE row carries `raw`, a non-null `canonical`, `role`, `component`, `operation`, `parameter`, `axes`, `layer`, `expert`. A NEGATIVE row carries `raw`, `canonical: null`, `why`, and — for an implemented family — `control`, the raw name of a POSITIVE row in the same family that must still resolve. The control is what stops a negative row from passing vacuously: against an empty rule table the negative would still say `unknown`, but its control would stop resolving and the assertion fails.",

  "_provenance": "No expected value here was produced by running the resolver. Every `canonical` was written by hand from the address rule below, whose shape is fixed by the ARCHITECTURE.md section 6.1 example `model.layers[10].self_attention.query_projection.weight` and whose component and operation vocabulary is fixed by ARCHITECTURE.md section 4.2 (`component: attention`, `operation: query_projection`, `axes: [output_channel, input_channel]` for exactly that name) together with the declared `architectures/*/plugin.toml` rule tables, which are the resolver's INPUT rather than its output. Every Qwen row that also appears in fixtures/tiny-qwen-single/golden.json — the checked-in golden generated for QM-0010 — is cross-checked against it by `the_corpus_agrees_with_the_checked_in_qwen_fixture_golden_on_every_shared_raw_name`, so a transcription slip in either file fails the suite. Nothing here reaches the network.",

  "_canonical_address_rule": "model[.layers[N]].<component>[.experts[E]].<operation>[.<parameter>]  (ARCHITECTURE.md section 6.1)",

  "_component_segments": "attention -> self_attention (ARCHITECTURE.md section 6.1 verbatim); mlp -> mlp; moe -> moe; normalization -> normalization; router -> router; embedding -> embedding; output_head -> output_head.",

  "_fidelity": "exact",

  "_what_this_corpus_is_not": "It maps NAMES to declared labels. It establishes nothing about what any tensor means, has learned, or computes. `query_projection` is the checkpoint author's word propagated through a declared rule table, not a finding about the weights (ARCHITECTURE.md section 19). No row was produced from, or is validated against, a real checkpoint: no Qwen, Llama, Kimi or DeepSeek checkpoint is committed to this repository and none is downloaded.",

